@muhammad: In many times and places, businesses are required to record, thus vendors adopt.

Do you have a specific example to share with me?

Benjamin Curtis said:

@muhammad: GDPR, HITRUST, SOC

These are regulations, right? Is there any company already logging it in a way proposed?

Benjamin Curtis said:

@muhammad, No standard that I am aware of, so no companies using one. Certainly a question for this BOF.

Thank you Benjamin.

Rich Salz said:

@MikeO Do you really expect an LLM audit log that generated a PR would be useful, in terms of validating the utility of the PR?

Yeah, I actually do. Knowing that the LLM cross-referenced a long-list of RFCs, ran a pile of skills, ran all the unit tests, etc, would give me much more confidence in the PR and tell it apart from a pile of code that was hallucinated into being without any of that diligence.

Joshua Moffat said:

@mike the alternative may be that the tech oligopoly owns your privacy...

They already do. Doesn't mean that we should standardize and endorse protocols that make it easier for them.
